IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (Western Australia) -- whether the Act covers my tenancy (s 5), what I must be given at
-- the start and the end (ss 27B, 27C), what I can be asked to pay (ss 27, 28), the security bond and where it must go
-- (ss 29, 31), how often and how my rent may rise (ss 30, 31B, 99), retaliation (s 26B), how my lessor and I may end the
-- tenancy (ss 60-70A, 76C, 80), and getting my bond back (ss 81C-81K).
--
-- SEAT: the tenant. Every decision is phrased as the tenant would ask it: "Where must my bond go?", "How often may my rent
-- rise?", "What must I be given?", "How much notice must my lessor give me?", "How much notice must I give?". Where the Act
-- hands a judgment to a court or the Commissioner (s 26B(4), s 64(4), s 65(2), s 81R), the answer is conditional on that
-- judgment, which is asked as a fact, or the decision says only that I may apply.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 3 ("residential tenancy agreement", "security bond", "rent", "expiry day"), s 5(1A), (2), (3), (4),
-- s 26A, s 26B(2), (3), s 27(1), (2)(a), (b), s 27B, s 27C(1)-(5), s 28(1), s 29(1), (2), (2A), (4)(a), (b), (5), s 30(1)-(3),
-- s 31(1A)-(2), s 31B, s 60(1)(a), (b), s 61, s 62(1)-(6), s 63, s 64(1)-(3), (5), s 65(1), s 68, s 69(1)(b), (2), (3),
-- s 70A(2)-(6), s 76C(2), s 80, s 81C(3)-(5), s 81D(2), s 81E(1), (2), s 81I(1), s 81K, s 99.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49316), "Residential Tenancies Act 1987 with editorial changes as
-- at 29 Apr 2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49316.txt. Its compilation table ends with the
-- Statutes (Repeals and Minor Amendments) Act 2025 s 35 (26 Sep 2025); the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2024 Pt 2 is
-- shown in force in three tranches (16 May 2024, 29 Jul 2024, 28 Mar 2026).
-- Regulations used: Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989, consolidated version 05-ad0-00 (currency start 3 Sep 2026), as
-- deposited at ../../../residential-tenancies-regulations-1989/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49840.txt: regs 3 (as one
-- fact), 5B (as one fact), 5CB, 10AB, 10ABA, 10AD, 10A, 11, 11A.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part II (administration), Part III Division 1 and Division 2 (dispute procedure) except s 26B; s 27A (form
-- of the agreement); s 27AA (advertising); s 28(2); s 29(3) (a rent decrease in the first 6 months), (6), (9); s 31A (rent
-- calculated by income: returned as not covered); s 32 (excessive rent) except as one fact for s 65; ss 33-36; Part IV
-- Division 2 (standard terms: repairs, entry, quiet enjoyment), Divisions 2A and 2B (pets, modifications) except the pet
-- bond, Division 3; s 62(5)(b), (5a), (7); s 64(4) (what the court may order); s 66; s 67 beyond its form; ss 69(1)(a), (4),
-- 70; Part V Division 2A (family violence), Division 3 (social housing), Division 4 (court orders) except as the end of s
-- 60, ss 76-81B; Part 5A Division 3 (the Commissioner's decision) and s 81T; Part VIA (tenancy databases); Part VI;
-- Schedule 1. Service (s 85) is not modelled: every date is the day a notice was in fact given or received.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA)`

§§ `numbers and dates the Act and the Regulations turn on`

-- Compilation table: Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2024 "s. 11, 12, 13(1), 14, 15(1), 18, 25-31, ... : 29 Jul 2024".
-- Section 25 of that Act amended s 30; s 99 and s 100 speak of "the day on which the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act
-- 2024 section 25 comes into operation".
`the day the 2024 rent rules commenced` MEANS Date 29 7 2024

-- s 28(1): "an amount exceeding 2 weeks' rent".
`weeks of rent payable in advance` MEANS 2

-- s 29(1)(b)(i) and s 31(2)(a): "4 weeks' rent".
`weeks of rent a bond may be` MEANS 4

-- Regulations reg 10A: "For the purposes of section 29(1)(b)(ii) of the Act, the amount of $350 is prescribed."
`the pet bond amount` MEANS 350

-- Regulations reg 11: "The amount of $1 200 is prescribed for the purposes of section 29(2) of the Act."
`the weekly rent above which the bond limit does not apply` MEANS 1200

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or after` MEANS Day `a` AT LEAST Day `b`

GIVEN `from` IS A DATE
      `n`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` MEANS Date (Day `from` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `earlier` IS A DATE
      `later`   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days between` MEANS Day `later` MINUS Day `earlier`

-- `the later of` and `the earlier of` (two dates) come from the daydate library.

§§ `5 -- does the Act cover my tenancy`

-- s 3: "residential tenancy agreement means any agreement, whether or not in writing and whether express or implied, under
-- which any person for valuable consideration grants to any other person a right to occupy, whether exclusively or
-- otherwise, any residential premises, or part of residential premises, for the purpose of residence".
-- s 5(1A): the Act "does not apply to a residential tenancy agreement that is a strata lease".
-- s 5(2): it does not apply "(a) where the tenant is a party to an agreement for the sale and purchase of the premises,
-- unless the period of the tenancy is one month or longer; (b) where the agreement arises under a mortgage ...; (c) [a
-- company-title scheme]; (d) where the tenant is a boarder or lodger; (e) where the agreement is bona fide entered into for
-- the purpose of conferring on a person a right to occupy premises for a holiday; (f), (g) [prescribed]".
-- s 5(3): nor to "(a) any part of a hotel or motel; (b) accommodation for students provided (i) by an educational
-- institution; or (ii) by an entity ... other than for the purpose of making a profit, unless ... prescribed; (ca) any part
-- of a hospital or nursing home; (c) any premises used for the purposes of a club; (d) ... residential care to approved care
-- recipients ...; (e) any prescribed premises".
-- s 5(4): "an agreement conferring a right to occupy premises for a fixed term of 3 months or longer shall be deemed, in
-- the absence of proof to the contrary, not to have been entered into bona fide for the purpose of conferring a right to
-- occupy the premises for a holiday."
-- "Boarder or lodger", "hotel", "club" are not defined in the Act: borrowed terms, asked as facts. Exclusions made by the
-- Regulations (reg 3 retirement villages, reg 4 squatters, regs 5, 5D Crown land) are one fact.
DECLARE `My arrangement` HAS
    `I pay rent or other value to occupy premises as my home`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 3
    `it is a strata lease`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(1A)
    `I am buying the premises under a contract of sale`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(a)
    `my tenancy is for one month or longer`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(a)
    `it arises under a mortgage of the premises`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(b)
    `it is a company-title scheme the tenants jointly control`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(c)
    `I am a boarder or lodger`                                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(d)
    `it was genuinely entered into for a holiday`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(e)
    `it is for a fixed term of 3 months or longer`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(4)
    `it is proved to be for a holiday despite the term`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(4): "proof to the contrary"
    `it is in a hotel, motel, hospital, nursing home or club`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(3)(a), (ca), (c)
    `it is non-profit or institutional student accommodation, not prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 5(3)(b)
    `it is residential aged care`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(3)(d)
    `the Regulations exclude it`                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 5(2)(f), (g), (3)(e); regs 3-5D

GIVEN `a` IS A `My arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is excluded as a holiday letting` MEANS
        `a`'s `it was genuinely entered into for a holiday`
    AND (    (NOT `a`'s `it is for a fixed term of 3 months or longer`)
         OR  `a`'s `it is proved to be for a holiday despite the term`)

@export Does the Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) apply to my tenancy (s 3, s 5)?
GIVEN `my arrangement` IS A `My arrangement` @desc What you pay, what kind of place it is, and the kind of arrangement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my tenancy` IF
        `my arrangement`'s `I pay rent or other value to occupy premises as my home`
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `it is a strata lease`)
    AND (NOT (`my arrangement`'s `I am buying the premises under a contract of sale` AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `my tenancy is for one month or longer`)))
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `it arises under a mortgage of the premises`)
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `it is a company-title scheme the tenants jointly control`)
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `I am a boarder or lodger`)
    AND (NOT `it is excluded as a holiday letting` `my arrangement`)
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `it is in a hotel, motel, hospital, nursing home or club`)
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `it is non-profit or institutional student accommodation, not prescribed`)
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `it is residential aged care`)
    AND (NOT `my arrangement`'s `the Regulations exclude it`)

§§ `27B, 27C -- what I must be given at the start and the end`

-- s 27B: "A lessor or property manager must give a copy of the information (if any) prescribed for the purposes of this
-- section to each tenant -- (a) in the case of a written residential tenancy agreement, at the time of entering into the
-- agreement; or (b) in any other case, within 14 days after the tenant has taken possession of the residential premises."
-- Regulations reg 10AB prescribes the information; reg 10ABA(1) requires it in the approved form on the same timing;
-- reg 10ABA(2): it "does not apply ... if (a) the agreement is renewed or extended; and (b) there has been no change in the
-- parties to the agreement".
@export Must I be given the prescribed tenancy information (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27B; Regulations reg 10ABA)?
GIVEN `my agreement is a renewal or extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this agreement renews or extends an earlier one
      `the parties have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any lessor or tenant is different from the earlier agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given the prescribed tenancy information` IF
        (NOT `my agreement is a renewal or extension`)
    OR  `the parties have changed`

@export By when must I be given the prescribed tenancy information (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27B)?
GIVEN `my agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a written tenancy agreement
      `the day I entered into the agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day you signed (entered into) the agreement
      `the day I took possession` IS A DATE @desc The day you took possession of the home
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I be given the prescribed tenancy information` IS
    IF `my agreement is in writing`
    THEN `the day I entered into the agreement`
    ELSE `days after` `the day I took possession` 14

-- s 27C(1): "A lessor or property manager must, within 7 days after a tenant has entered into occupation ... (a) prepare a
-- report describing the condition of the premises; and (b) provide 2 copies of the report to the tenant."
-- Regulations reg 10AC: the report's contents are Schedule 4 Form 1.
@export By when must I be given two copies of the property condition report (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27C(1))?
GIVEN `the day I moved in` IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into occupation of the premises
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I be given the property condition report` IS
    `days after` `the day I moved in` 7

-- s 27C(2): "A tenant given copies of a report under subsection (1)(b) who disagrees with any information in the report
-- must, within 7 days of receiving the copies -- (a) mark a copy ...; and (b) give the copy back".
@export By when must I give back a marked copy of the property condition report (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27C(2))?
GIVEN `the day I received the copies` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the two copies of the report
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I return my marked copy of the report` IS
    `days after` `the day I received the copies` 7

-- s 27C(3): "If the tenant does not give a copy of the report back to the lessor or property manager under subsection (2),
-- the tenant is to be taken to accept the report as a true and accurate description of the condition of the residential
-- premises." A copy given back after the 7 days is not given back "under subsection (2)" (INFERENCE).
@export Am I taken to accept the property condition report as accurate (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27C(3))?
GIVEN `the day I received the copies` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the two copies of the report
      `I gave back a marked copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave back a copy marked to show what you disagree with
      `the day I gave it back` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the marked copy back (ignored if you did not)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to accept the condition report` IF
        (NOT `I gave back a marked copy`)
    OR  `is on or after` `the day I gave it back` (`days after` `the day I received the copies` 8)

-- s 27C(4): "A lessor or property manager must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 14 days, after the
-- termination of a tenancy ... (a) conduct an inspection ...; (b) prepare a final report ...; (c) provide a copy of the
-- report to the tenant." s 27C(5): "The tenant is to be given a reasonable opportunity to be present at the inspection".
@export By when must I be given the final property condition report (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27C(4))?
GIVEN `the day my tenancy ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your tenancy (or your interest in it) terminated
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I be given the final condition report` IS
    `days after` `the day my tenancy ended` 14

§§ `27, 28 -- what I can be asked to pay`

-- s 27(1): "A person must not require or receive from a tenant any monetary amount for or in relation to a residential
-- tenancy agreement other than rent and a security bond." s 27(2): not "(a) any amount, not exceeding a prescribed amount,
-- required or received as consideration for an option to enter into a residential tenancy agreement if (i) upon the option
-- being exercised, the amount is refunded in cash or applied towards the rent ...; or (ii) upon the option being refused,
-- and within 7 days ..., the amount is refunded ...; (b) any amount that the lessor is authorised by any other provision of
-- this Act to require or receive; (d) any other payment of a prescribed class."
DECLARE `A payment asked of me` IS ONE OF
    `rent`                                                          -- s 27(1)
    `a security bond`                                               -- s 27(1)
    `an option fee, to be refunded or applied to rent`              -- s 27(2)(a)
    `an amount another provision of the Act authorises`             -- s 27(2)(b), for example a utility charge (s 49A)
    `any other amount, such as a letting fee or key money`          -- s 27(1)

-- Regulations reg 10AD, Table: "Where the weekly rent ... is $500 or less: $50"; "Where the weekly rent ... exceeds $500:
-- $100"; "Where the residential tenancy agreement is for residential premises south of the 26th parallel of south latitude
-- and the weekly rent is $1 200 or more: $1 200". The second and third rows overlap; the third, more particular row is
-- read as governing where both describe the agreement (INFERENCE).
@export What is the most I can be charged for an option to rent (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27(2)(a); Regulations reg 10AD)?
GIVEN `the weekly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rent, in dollars
      `the home is south of the 26th parallel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the premises are south of latitude 26 degrees south (Perth is)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most an option fee may be` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `the home is south of the 26th parallel` AND `the weekly rent` AT LEAST 1200 THEN 1200
      IF `the weekly rent` AT MOST 500 THEN 50
      OTHERWISE 100

@export May I be asked to pay this (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 27)?
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `A payment asked of me` @desc What the payment is for
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount asked, in dollars
      `the weekly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rent, in dollars
      `the home is south of the 26th parallel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the premises are south of latitude 26 degrees south
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be asked to pay this` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `an option fee, to be refunded or applied to rent` THEN
        `the amount` AT MOST `the most an option fee may be` `the weekly rent` `the home is south of the 26th parallel`
    WHEN `any other amount, such as a letting fee or key money` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 28(1): "A person must not require before or during the first 2 weeks of the tenancy ... as rent ... an amount
-- exceeding 2 weeks' rent."
@export What is the most rent I can be asked to pay up front (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 28(1))?
GIVEN `the weekly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rent, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most rent I can be asked to pay in advance` IS
    `the weekly rent` TIMES `weeks of rent payable in advance`

§§ `29 -- my security bond, and where it must go`

-- s 29(1): "A person must not -- (a) require the payment of, or receive, more than one security bond in relation to any
-- residential tenancy agreement; or (b) require the payment of, or receive, a security bond of an amount exceeding in the
-- aggregate -- (i) 4 weeks' rent ...; and (ii) if the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises -- a prescribed
-- amount [$350, reg 10A] ..." s 29(2A): "(1)(a) does not prevent a person from receiving a security bond in instalments."
-- s 29(2): "(1)(b) does not apply ... where the weekly rate of rent ... exceeds a prescribed amount" [$1 200, reg 11].
@export What is the most security bond I can be asked for (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 29(1)(b); Regulations reg 10A)?
GIVEN `the weekly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rent, in dollars
      `I am permitted to keep a pet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are permitted to keep a pet at the premises
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most security bond I can be asked for` IS
    `the weekly rent` TIMES `weeks of rent a bond may be`
        PLUS (IF `I am permitted to keep a pet` THEN `the pet bond amount` ELSE 0)

@export Does the limit on the bond apply to my tenancy (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 29(2); Regulations reg 11)?
GIVEN `the weekly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rent, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the bond limit apply to me` IF
    `the weekly rent` AT MOST `the weekly rent above which the bond limit does not apply`

@export Is the bond I am asked for within the law (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 29(1), (2), (2A))?
GIVEN `the weekly rent` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rent, in dollars
      `I am permitted to keep a pet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are permitted to keep a pet at the premises
      `the bond asked` IS A NUMBER @desc The total security bond asked (all instalments), in dollars
      `the number of separate bonds asked` IS A NUMBER @desc How many separate security bonds are asked for this agreement (instalments of one bond count as one)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my bond within the law` IF
        `the number of separate bonds asked` AT MOST 1
    AND (    (NOT `Does the bond limit apply to me` `the weekly rent`)
         OR  `the bond asked` AT MOST `the most security bond I can be asked for` `the weekly rent` `I am permitted to keep a pet`)

-- s 29(4): "A person who receives a security bond ... (a) must, as soon as practicable, give the person who paid the bond a
-- receipt stating ... (i) the date on which the bond was received; (ii) the name of the person who paid the bond; (iii) the
-- amount of bond paid; (iv) the premises to which the bond relates; and (b) must pay the bond to the bond administrator as
-- soon as practicable, and in any event within 14 days, after the day on which the person received the bond; and (c) must
-- ... lodge a record of the payment, in the approved form". Penalty: a fine of $20 000.
-- s 3: "bond administrator means the chief executive officer of the Department".
@export By when must my bond reach the bond administrator (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 29(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the bond was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the lessor or property manager received your bond (or an instalment)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must my bond be paid to the bond administrator` IS
    `days after` `the day the bond was received` 14

DECLARE `My bond receipt` HAS
    `it states the date the bond was received`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 29(4)(a)(i)
    `it states who paid it`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 29(4)(a)(ii)
    `it states the amount`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 29(4)(a)(iii)
    `it states the premises`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 29(4)(a)(iv)

@export Does my bond receipt state what it must (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 29(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the receipt` IS A `My bond receipt` @desc What your receipt states
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my bond receipt state what it must` IF
        `the receipt`'s `it states the date the bond was received`
    AND `the receipt`'s `it states who paid it`
    AND `the receipt`'s `it states the amount`
    AND `the receipt`'s `it states the premises`

-- s 29(5): "A security bond must be paid to the bond administrator under subsection (4)(b) in a prescribed way."
-- Regulations reg 11A(2): "If the premises are not managed by a property manager, the security bond must be paid to the
-- bond administrator in an approved way." reg 11A(3): if managed by a property manager, "(a) if subregulation (4) applies
-- -- in an approved way but not by using BondsOnline eTransactions; or (b) otherwise -- using BondsOnline eTransactions."
-- reg 11A(4): applies if "(a) the tenant does not have 1 or more of the following -- (i) a mobile telephone number used
-- exclusively by the tenant; (ii) an email address used exclusively by the tenant; (iii) internet access ...; (iv)
-- competence in the use of a mobile telephone or email; (v) a sound understanding of the English language; or (b) the bond
-- administrator has agreed to the payment being made in accordance with subregulation (3)(a)."
DECLARE `Where my bond must go` IS ONE OF
    `to the bond administrator, through BondsOnline eTransactions`
    `to the bond administrator, in an approved way other than BondsOnline eTransactions`
    `to the bond administrator, in an approved way`

@export Where must my bond go (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 29(4)(b), (5); Regulations reg 11A)?
GIVEN `a property manager manages the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensed real estate agent manages the premises for the lessor
      `I lack an exclusive mobile, exclusive email, internet access, competence with them, or sound English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lack at least one of the things in reg 11A(4)(a)
      `the bond administrator agreed to another way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bond administrator has agreed to payment other than through BondsOnline
GIVETH A `Where my bond must go`
DECIDE `Where must my bond go` IS
    BRANCH
      IF (NOT `a property manager manages the premises`)
        THEN `to the bond administrator, in an approved way`
      IF `I lack an exclusive mobile, exclusive email, internet access, competence with them, or sound English`
          OR `the bond administrator agreed to another way`
        THEN `to the bond administrator, in an approved way other than BondsOnline eTransactions`
      OTHERWISE `to the bond administrator, through BondsOnline eTransactions`

§§ `30, 31B, 99 -- how often and how my rent may rise`

-- s 30(1): "Subject to this section and except where rent ... is calculated by reference to the tenant's income, the rent
-- ... may be increased by the lessor by written notice to the tenant, in the approved form, specifying the amount of the
-- increased rent and the day as from which the increased rent becomes payable, being a day -- (a) not less than 60 days
-- after the day on which the notice is given; and (b) not less than 12 months after the day on which the tenancy commenced,
-- or, if the rent has been increased under this section, the day on which it was last so increased, but otherwise the rent
-- shall not increase or be increased."
-- s 30(2): the right "(a) is not exercisable in relation to a residential tenancy agreement that creates a tenancy for a
-- fixed term during the currency of that term unless the amount of the increase, or the method of calculating the amount
-- of the increase, is set out in the agreement; and (b) in any case, may be excluded or limited by agreement".
-- s 30(3): a notice given in accordance with the section and not withdrawn "varies the residential tenancy agreement".
-- s 99: for a fixed term "entered into, or last renewed or extended, before the commencement" whose current term "ends after
-- the commencement", "Section 30, as in force from time to time before the commencement, continues to apply ... until the
-- end of the current term". The former s 30 is not in the deposit, so that case is returned as not covered.
-- Regulations reg 5B: s 30(1) does not apply to agreements with listed employers and agencies (one fact).
DECLARE `My rent increase notice` HAS
    `it is in writing in the approved form`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(1)
    `it states the new rent and the day it starts`          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(1)
    `the day it was given`                                  IS A DATE     -- s 30(1)(a)
    `the day the new rent starts`                           IS A DATE     -- s 30(1)

DECLARE `My tenancy, for a rent increase` HAS
    `my rent is calculated by reference to my income`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(1), s 31A
    `regulation 5B exempts my agreement`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 5B
    `the day my tenancy commenced`                          IS A DATE     -- s 30(1)(b), reckoned under s 31B
    `my rent has been increased under section 30`           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(1)(b)
    `the day it was last increased`                         IS A DATE     -- s 30(1)(b)
    `I have a fixed term`                                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(2)(a)
    `the day my current term was entered, renewed or extended` IS A DATE  -- s 99(2)(a)
    `the day my current term ends`                          IS A DATE     -- s 30(2)(a), s 99(2)(b)
    `the agreement sets out the increase or how to work it out` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 30(2)(a)
    `the agreement excludes or limits this increase`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 30(2)(b)

DECLARE `What becomes of my rent increase` IS ONE OF
    `the new rent is payable from the day in the notice`
    `not covered: my rent is calculated by my income, so section 31A governs`
    `not covered: regulation 5B takes my agreement out of section 30(1)`
    `not covered: section 99 keeps the former section 30 for my current fixed term`
    `no effect: the notice is not in writing in the approved form stating the new rent and its day`
    `no effect: my fixed term does not set out the increase or how to work it out`
    `no effect: my agreement excludes or limits this increase`
    `no effect: the new rent starts less than 60 days after the notice`
    `no effect: the new rent starts less than 12 months after my tenancy began or the rent last rose`

GIVEN `t` IS A `My tenancy, for a rent increase`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the 12 months run from` MEANS
    IF `t`'s `my rent has been increased under section 30`
    THEN `t`'s `the day it was last increased`
    ELSE `t`'s `the day my tenancy commenced`

@export What is the earliest day my rent can go up (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 30(1))?
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc The day the rent increase notice is (or will be) given to you
      `the day my tenancy commenced or the rent last rose` IS A DATE @desc The day your tenancy began or, if the rent has been increased under s 30, the day it was last increased
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the earliest day my rent can go up` IS
    `the later of` (`days after` `the day the notice is given` 60) (`add months` `the day my tenancy commenced or the rent last rose` 12)

@export Is this rent increase valid (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30, 99)?
GIVEN `the notice` IS A `My rent increase notice` @desc The rent increase notice you were given
      `my tenancy` IS A `My tenancy, for a rent increase` @desc Your tenancy's dates and terms
GIVETH A `What becomes of my rent increase`
DECIDE `Is my rent increase valid` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `my tenancy`'s `my rent is calculated by reference to my income`
        THEN `not covered: my rent is calculated by my income, so section 31A governs`
      IF `my tenancy`'s `regulation 5B exempts my agreement`
        THEN `not covered: regulation 5B takes my agreement out of section 30(1)`
      IF `my tenancy`'s `I have a fixed term`
          AND (NOT `is on or after` (`my tenancy`'s `the day my current term was entered, renewed or extended`) `the day the 2024 rent rules commenced`)
          AND (NOT `is on or after` `the day the 2024 rent rules commenced` (`my tenancy`'s `the day my current term ends`))
          AND `is on or after` (`my tenancy`'s `the day my current term ends`) (`the notice`'s `the day the new rent starts`)
        THEN `not covered: section 99 keeps the former section 30 for my current fixed term`
      IF (NOT (`the notice`'s `it is in writing in the approved form` AND `the notice`'s `it states the new rent and the day it starts`))
        THEN `no effect: the notice is not in writing in the approved form stating the new rent and its day`
      IF `my tenancy`'s `I have a fixed term`
          AND `is on or after` (`my tenancy`'s `the day my current term ends`) (`the notice`'s `the day the new rent starts`)
          AND (NOT `my tenancy`'s `the agreement sets out the increase or how to work it out`)
        THEN `no effect: my fixed term does not set out the increase or how to work it out`
      IF `my tenancy`'s `the agreement excludes or limits this increase`
        THEN `no effect: my agreement excludes or limits this increase`
      IF (NOT `is on or after` (`the notice`'s `the day the new rent starts`) (`days after` (`the notice`'s `the day it was given`) 60))
        THEN `no effect: the new rent starts less than 60 days after the notice`
      IF (NOT `is on or after` (`the notice`'s `the day the new rent starts`) (`add months` (`the day the 12 months run from` `my tenancy`) 12))
        THEN `no effect: the new rent starts less than 12 months after my tenancy began or the rent last rose`
      OTHERWISE `the new rent is payable from the day in the notice`

-- s 31B(2): a new agreement "is taken to be a continuation of another ... if the continuing agreement -- (a) is between the
-- same parties as the existing agreement; and (b) is for the same residential premises ...; and (c) starts immediately after
-- the end of the term of the existing agreement." s 31B(3): the same parties if "(a) the lessor is the same under both
-- agreements; and (b) the tenant, or at least 1 cotenant, is the same". So signing a new lease does not restart the 12 months.
@export Does my new agreement count as a continuation of my old one, for rent increases (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 31B)?
GIVEN `the lessor is the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lessor is the same under both agreements
      `at least one tenant is the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or at least one cotenant, are tenants under both
      `the premises are the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both agreements are for the same home
      `it starts immediately after the old term ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new agreement starts straight after the old term ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my new agreement a continuation of my old one` IF
        `the lessor is the same` AND `at least one tenant is the same`
    AND `the premises are the same`
    AND `it starts immediately after the old term ends`

§§ `31 -- may my bond be increased`

-- s 31(1A): "If a notice of increase in rent is given under section 30 or 31A ..., the lessor may increase the amount of the
-- security bond ... by giving the tenant a written notice that states (a) the amount by which the security bond is increased
-- ...; and (b) the day on which the additional amount is payable." Regulations reg 5CB widens the trigger to a "relevant
-- event", which includes the lessor's approval (or deemed approval, or the Commissioner's order) to keep a pet.
-- s 31(1B) (as modified by reg 5CB(c)): the day "cannot be a day (a) earlier than 60 days after the day on which the notice
-- under subsection (1A) is given; or (b) if a notice of increase of rent is given ... -- before the rent increase ... takes
-- effect." s 31(2): not "to an amount that would exceed the aggregate of (a) 4 weeks' rent ... at the time at which the
-- amount of the increase would be payable; and (b) any amount provided for by section 29(1)(b)(ii)". s 31(2) has no
-- exception for rent above $1 200 a week.
DECLARE `My bond increase` HAS
    `it follows a rent increase notice`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 31(1A); reg 5CB(1AA)(a)
    `it follows approval to keep a pet`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- reg 5CB(1AA)(b)-(d)
    `the notice is in writing and states the amount and the day` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 31(1A)
    `the day the bond notice was given`                     IS A DATE     -- s 31(1B)(a)
    `the day the extra bond is payable`                     IS A DATE     -- s 31(1A)(b)
    `the day the rent increase takes effect`                IS A DATE     -- s 31(1B)(b)
    `the new total bond`                                    IS A NUMBER   -- s 31(2)
    `the weekly rent when the extra bond is payable`        IS A NUMBER   -- s 31(2)(a)
    `I am permitted to keep a pet`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 31(2)(b)

@export May my bond be increased as my lessor proposes (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 31; Regulations reg 5CB)?
GIVEN `the increase` IS A `My bond increase` @desc The proposed increase in your security bond
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my bond be increased this way` IF
        (`the increase`'s `it follows a rent increase notice` OR `the increase`'s `it follows approval to keep a pet`)
    AND `the increase`'s `the notice is in writing and states the amount and the day`
    AND `is on or after` (`the increase`'s `the day the extra bond is payable`) (`days after` (`the increase`'s `the day the bond notice was given`) 60)
    AND (    (NOT `the increase`'s `it follows a rent increase notice`)
         OR  `is on or after` (`the increase`'s `the day the extra bond is payable`) (`the increase`'s `the day the rent increase takes effect`))
    AND `the increase`'s `the new total bond` AT MOST
            (`the increase`'s `the weekly rent when the extra bond is payable` TIMES `weeks of rent a bond may be`
                PLUS (IF `the increase`'s `I am permitted to keep a pet` THEN `the pet bond amount` ELSE 0))

§§ `26A, 26B -- retaliation`

-- s 26A: the lessor takes retaliatory action if it "(a) ... (i) gives the tenant a notice claiming the tenant has breached
-- the residential tenancy agreement, other than by failing to pay rent ...; (ii) increases the rent ...; (iii) takes action
-- to terminate the residential tenancy agreement; (iv) at the end of the current residential tenancy agreement, refuses to
-- enter into a further residential tenancy agreement ...; and (b) is motivated to take the action, wholly or partly, by the
-- matter arising." s 26B(2): the section applies "if a tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action against
-- the tenant after" the tenant enforced their rights, complained to a government entity, or a court order is in force.
-- s 26B(3): "The tenant may apply to a competent court for relief". What the court orders (s 26B(4)) is its judgment.
@export May I ask a court for relief because my lessor is retaliating (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26B)?
GIVEN `the lessor gave a breach notice (not for rent), raised the rent, moved to end my tenancy, or refused a new agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lessor took one of the actions in s 26A(a)
      `I had enforced my rights, complained to a government entity, or a court order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the matters in s 26B(2)(a)-(c) arose before the action
      `I reasonably believe the action was motivated by that` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably believe the lessor acted wholly or partly because of that matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for relief from retaliatory action` IF
        `the lessor gave a breach notice (not for rent), raised the rent, moved to end my tenancy, or refused a new agreement`
    AND `I had enforced my rights, complained to a government entity, or a court order is in force`
    AND `I reasonably believe the action was motivated by that`

§§ `60-65, 69, 70A -- how my lessor may end my tenancy`

-- s 60(1): an agreement "shall not terminate or be terminated except" in listed circumstances, the first being "where the
-- lessor or tenant gives notice of termination under this Act and (i) the tenant delivers up vacant possession ... on or
-- after the expiration of the period of notice ...; or (ii) a competent court, upon application by the lessor, terminates
-- the agreement under section 71". s 80: "No person shall except under an order of a competent court enter premises ... of
-- which a person has possession as a tenant ... for the purpose of recovering possession ..., whether entry is effected
-- peaceably or otherwise." Penalty: a fine of $20 000.
@export May my lessor enter and take back my home without a court order (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 60, 80)?
GIVEN `a court has ordered possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a competent court has made an order for possession against you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my lessor enter to recover possession` IF
    `a court has ordered possession`

DECLARE `My lessor's ground` IS ONE OF
    `I breached a term other than paying rent, and have not remedied it`   -- s 62(1), (3)
    `I have not paid rent`                                                 -- s 62(1), (4), (5)
    `the lessor has contracted to sell with vacant possession`             -- s 63
    `no ground`                                                            -- s 64
    `the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or compulsorily acquired`   -- s 69
    `my fixed term is ending`                                              -- s 70A

-- s 62(2): "not less than 7 days"; s 63(2): "not less than 30 days"; s 64(2): "not less than 60 days"; s 69(2): "not less
-- than 7 days"; s 70A(3): "not later than 30 days before the possession day" -- each before the day the tenant must give
-- possession.
@export How many days' notice must my lessor give me (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 62-64, 69, 70A)?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `My lessor's ground` @desc The ground on which the lessor ends the tenancy
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days notice must my lessor give me` IS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `I breached a term other than paying rent, and have not remedied it` THEN 7
    WHEN `I have not paid rent` THEN 7
    WHEN `the lessor has contracted to sell with vacant possession` THEN 30
    WHEN `no ground` THEN 60
    WHEN `the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or compulsorily acquired` THEN 7
    WHEN `my fixed term is ending` THEN 30

-- s 61: "Notice of termination ... by the lessor must -- (a) be in writing and in the prescribed form; and (b) be signed by
-- the lessor or a property manager ...; and (c) identify the premises ...; and (d) specify the day on which possession of the
-- premises is to be delivered up by the tenant; and (e) specify and give particulars of the ground, if any".
-- s 62(3): for a breach other than rent "the notice is ineffectual unless a notice specifying the breach and requiring that
-- it be remedied is given to the tenant not less than 14 days before the notice of termination is given." s 62(4)(a): the
-- same for rent, but s 62(5): "Despite subsection (4)(a), notice of termination upon the ground of a breach of the agreement
-- to pay rent may be given immediately the breach occurs but where notice is so given -- (a) the lessor shall not make an
-- application under section 71 if the rent due ... is paid in full before the day specified in the notice". A rent notice
-- without the 14-day notice is read as a s 62(5) notice (INFERENCE).
-- s 63(4) and s 64(5): those sections do not apply "to a residential tenancy agreement that creates a tenancy for a fixed
-- term during the currency of that term". s 62(6), s 69(4): a breach or frustration notice may name a day before the term
-- ends. s 70A(4): "The possession day must not be a day earlier than the expiry day."
-- s 65(1): while proceedings are pending, or an order is in force, under s 32 fixing the maximum rent, "(a) any notice of
-- termination ... under section 64 is ineffectual; and (b) any other notice ... is ineffectual unless first authorised by a
-- competent court".
DECLARE `My lessor's notice` HAS
    `it is in writing in the prescribed form and signed by the lessor or property manager` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 61(a), (b)
    `it identifies the premises and the day I must leave`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 61(c), (d)
    `it gives particulars of the ground`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 61(e)
    `the day it was given`                                 IS A DATE
    `the day I must give possession`                       IS A DATE
    `a notice to remedy was given first`                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 62(3), (4)(a)
    `the day the notice to remedy was given`               IS A DATE

DECLARE `My tenancy, for a notice` HAS
    `I am within a fixed term`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the expiry day`                                       IS A DATE     -- s 3 "expiry day"
    `excessive-rent proceedings are pending or an order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 65(1)
    `a court authorised the notice under section 65(2)`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 65(2)

DECLARE `What my lessor's notice does` IS ONE OF
    `valid: if I have not left by the day it names, my lessor must apply to a court`
    `valid as an immediate rent notice: if I pay all rent owing before the day it names, my lessor may not apply to a court`
    `ineffectual: not in the form section 61 requires`
    `ineffectual: this ground cannot end my fixed term during its currency`
    `ineffectual: there is no fixed term to end`
    `ineffectual: the possession day is earlier than the expiry day`
    `ineffectual: excessive-rent proceedings or an order (section 65)`
    `ineffectual: no notice to remedy was given at least 14 days before`
    `ineffectual: too little notice`

@export What does my lessor's notice of termination do (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 60-65, 69, 70A)?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `My lessor's ground` @desc The ground the notice gives
      `the notice` IS A `My lessor's notice` @desc The notice of termination you were given
      `my tenancy` IS A `My tenancy, for a notice` @desc Whether you are in a fixed term, its expiry day, and any excessive-rent proceedings
GIVETH A `What my lessor's notice does`
DECIDE `What does my lessor's notice do` IS
    BRANCH
      IF (NOT (`the notice`'s `it is in writing in the prescribed form and signed by the lessor or property manager`
               AND `the notice`'s `it identifies the premises and the day I must leave`
               AND (`the ground` EQUALS `no ground` OR `the notice`'s `it gives particulars of the ground`)))
        THEN `ineffectual: not in the form section 61 requires`
      IF `my tenancy`'s `I am within a fixed term`
          AND (`the ground` EQUALS `no ground` OR `the ground` EQUALS `the lessor has contracted to sell with vacant possession`)
        THEN `ineffectual: this ground cannot end my fixed term during its currency`
      IF `the ground` EQUALS `my fixed term is ending` AND (NOT `my tenancy`'s `I am within a fixed term`)
        THEN `ineffectual: there is no fixed term to end`
      IF `the ground` EQUALS `my fixed term is ending`
          AND (NOT `is on or after` (`the notice`'s `the day I must give possession`) (`my tenancy`'s `the expiry day`))
        THEN `ineffectual: the possession day is earlier than the expiry day`
      IF `my tenancy`'s `excessive-rent proceedings are pending or an order is in force`
          AND (`the ground` EQUALS `no ground` OR (NOT `my tenancy`'s `a court authorised the notice under section 65(2)`))
        THEN `ineffectual: excessive-rent proceedings or an order (section 65)`
      IF `the ground` EQUALS `I breached a term other than paying rent, and have not remedied it`
          AND (NOT (`the notice`'s `a notice to remedy was given first`
                    AND `days between` (`the notice`'s `the day the notice to remedy was given`) (`the notice`'s `the day it was given`) AT LEAST 14))
        THEN `ineffectual: no notice to remedy was given at least 14 days before`
      IF `days between` (`the notice`'s `the day it was given`) (`the notice`'s `the day I must give possession`)
           LESS THAN `How many days notice must my lessor give me` `the ground`
        THEN `ineffectual: too little notice`
      IF `the ground` EQUALS `I have not paid rent`
          AND (NOT (`the notice`'s `a notice to remedy was given first`
                    AND `days between` (`the notice`'s `the day the notice to remedy was given`) (`the notice`'s `the day it was given`) AT LEAST 14))
        THEN `valid as an immediate rent notice: if I pay all rent owing before the day it names, my lessor may not apply to a court`
      OTHERWISE `valid: if I have not left by the day it names, my lessor must apply to a court`

-- s 64(3): "A tenant may, within 7 days after receiving a notice of termination under this section, apply to a competent
-- court for an order that the period of notice be extended by a further period of up to 60 days." Whether to extend, refuse
-- termination, or order possession (s 64(4)) is the court's judgment "having regard to the justice and merits of the case".
@export By when must I apply to a court to extend a no-grounds notice (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(3))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the lessor's notice given without a ground
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to extend a no-grounds notice` IS
    `days after` `the day I received the notice` 7

@export What is the most extra time a court may give me on a no-grounds notice (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 64(3), (4)(a))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the most extra days a court may give me on a no-grounds notice` IS 60

§§ `67-70A, 76C -- how I may end my tenancy, and the end of a fixed term`

-- s 68(1): "A tenant may give notice of termination ... without specifying any ground". s 68(2): "not less than 21 days
-- before the termination day". s 68(3): "This section does not apply in relation to a residential tenancy agreement that
-- creates a tenancy for a fixed term during the currency of that term."
-- s 69(3): where the premises are destroyed, uninhabitable or acquired, a tenant's notice "shall be not less than 2 days".
-- s 70A(3): a notice ending a fixed term "must be given not later than 30 days before the possession day".
-- s 67(1): the tenant's notice must "(a) be in writing; and (b) be signed by the tenant and identify the premises ...; and
-- (c) specify the day on which the tenant will deliver up possession".
-- Ending a fixed term early on the ground of family violence (Part V Division 2A) is not encoded.
DECLARE `My ground for ending` IS ONE OF
    `without a ground`                                                     -- s 68
    `the premises have become unusable or been acquired`   -- s 69(1)(b), (3)
    `to end my fixed term`                                              -- s 70A

@export May I end my tenancy by notice on this ground (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 68-70A)?
GIVEN `my ground` IS A `My ground for ending` @desc The ground on which you want to end the tenancy
      `I am within a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fixed term is still running
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I end my tenancy by notice on this ground` IF
    CONSIDER `my ground`
    WHEN `without a ground` THEN (NOT `I am within a fixed term`)
    WHEN `to end my fixed term` THEN `I am within a fixed term`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export How many days' notice must I give to end my tenancy (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 68, 69, 70A)?
GIVEN `my ground` IS A `My ground for ending` @desc The ground on which you end the tenancy
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days notice must I give` IS
    CONSIDER `my ground`
    WHEN `without a ground` THEN 21
    WHEN `the premises have become unusable or been acquired` THEN 2
    WHEN `to end my fixed term` THEN 30

@export Is my notice to end the tenancy valid (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 67-70A)?
GIVEN `my ground` IS A `My ground for ending` @desc The ground on which you end the tenancy
      `I am within a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your fixed term is still running
      `it is in writing, signed, and names the premises and the day I will leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your notice meets s 67(1)
      `the day I give notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you give the notice
      `the day I will leave` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice says you will deliver up possession
      `the expiry day` IS A DATE @desc The day your fixed term ends (ignored if you have none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice to end the tenancy valid` IF
        `May I end my tenancy by notice on this ground` `my ground` `I am within a fixed term`
    AND `it is in writing, signed, and names the premises and the day I will leave`
    AND `days between` `the day I give notice` `the day I will leave` AT LEAST `How many days notice must I give` `my ground`
    AND (    (NOT (`my ground` EQUALS `to end my fixed term`))
         OR  `is on or after` `the day I will leave` `the expiry day`)

@export What is the last day I can give notice to end my fixed term on its expiry day (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the expiry day` IS A DATE @desc The day your fixed term ends
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day to give notice ending my term on its expiry day` IS
    Date (Day `the expiry day` MINUS 30)

-- s 70A(2): "the term of a residential tenancy agreement does not end on the expiry day unless the lessor or tenant has given
-- a notice of termination ... specifying a day on which possession ... is to be delivered up". s 70A(5): "If the possession
-- day is later than the expiry day, then (a) the term of the agreement expires on the possession day, and not on the expiry
-- day". s 76C(2): the agreement "continues as a periodic tenancy after the expiry day on the same terms".
DECLARE `What happens at the end of my fixed term` IS ONE OF
    `it continues as a periodic tenancy on the same terms`
    `the term ends on the expiry day`
    `the term runs on to the possession day in the notice`

@export What happens to my tenancy when my fixed term expires (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 70A, 76C)?
GIVEN `a notice under section 70A was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or the lessor gave notice ending the fixed term
      `the expiry day` IS A DATE @desc The day the fixed term would end on its terms
      `the possession day` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice names for you to give possession (ignored if no notice)
GIVETH A `What happens at the end of my fixed term`
DECIDE `What happens when my fixed term expires` IS
    BRANCH
      IF (NOT `a notice under section 70A was given`) THEN `it continues as a periodic tenancy on the same terms`
      IF Day `the possession day` GREATER THAN Day `the expiry day` THEN `the term runs on to the possession day in the notice`
      OTHERWISE `the term ends on the expiry day`

-- s 70A(6): "If both the lessor and tenant give a notice to each other and the notices specify different possession days,
-- then the day that is the earlier of the 2 days is to be taken to be the possession day."
@export If my lessor and I both give notice ending the fixed term, which possession day counts (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 70A(6))?
GIVEN `my possession day` IS A DATE @desc The day your notice names
      `my lessor's possession day` IS A DATE @desc The day the lessor's notice names
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which possession day counts` IS
    `the earlier of` `my possession day` `my lessor's possession day`

§§ `81C-81K -- getting my bond back`

-- s 81C(3): a security bond release application "must not be made before the residential tenancy agreement terminates."
-- s 81C(4): "However, [it] may be made before the residential tenancy agreement terminates if (a) the tenant or, if there are
-- cotenants, all of the tenants deliver up vacant possession ...; and (b) the parties ... agree in writing to terminate".
-- s 81D(2): a partial release "only if (a) the rent payable ... has been reduced; or (b) the tenant paid the prescribed amount
-- under section 29(1)(b)(ii) in relation to a pet ... and the pet is no longer being kept on the premises; or (c) other
-- prescribed circumstances exist".
-- s 81C(5): "The lessor and property manager must not ask or require a tenant to sign a security bond release application
-- unless (a) the residential tenancy agreement has terminated or subsection (4) or section 81D applies; and (b) the
-- application states the amount of the security bond (if any) to be paid to the lessor and the tenant". Penalty: $5 000.
-- Part 5A commenced 28 March 2026 (compilation table, s 43 of No. 11 of 2024); s 101(2) applies it to agreements in force then.
@export May I be asked to sign a bond release application (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 81C(5), 81D)?
GIVEN `my agreement has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tenancy agreement has ended
      `all tenants have given vacant possession and the parties agreed in writing to end it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 81C(4) is met
      `the rent was reduced or my pet bond is no longer needed, and this is a partial release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 81D(2)(a) or (b) is met for a partial release
      `the application states how much goes to the lessor and to each tenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the form states the amounts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be asked to sign a bond release application` IF
        (    `my agreement has terminated`
         OR  `all tenants have given vacant possession and the parties agreed in writing to end it`
         OR  `the rent was reduced or my pet bond is no longer needed, and this is a partial release`)
    AND `the application states how much goes to the lessor and to each tenant`

-- s 81E(1): "A lessor is entitled to payment from the security bond ... of any of the following amounts -- (a) the reasonable
-- cost of repairs to the premises, or the restoration of the premises to their original condition, as a result of damage
-- (other than fair wear and tear) caused by the tenant, an occupant or an invitee ...; (b) [the same for chattels]; (c) any
-- rent or other charges owing and payable ...; (d) the cost of cleaning any part of the premises not left reasonably clean
-- ..., having regard to the condition of the premises at the start of the tenancy; (e) ... the cost of replacing locks or
-- other security devices altered, removed or added by the tenant without the consent of the lessor; (f) an amount the tenant
-- is liable to pay to the lessor for a breach of the agreement." s 81E(2): from the pet amount, pet damage, fumigation "if the
-- lessor considers it is necessary" because the pet "is capable of carrying parasites that can affect humans", and other
-- reasonable pet costs. s 81E(3): "(1) and (2) do not limit the matters for which the lessor may claim" -- so FALSE here
-- means only that the Act gives no entitlement; fair wear and tear is expressly excluded from (a) and (b).
DECLARE `A claim on my bond` IS ONE OF
    `repairs for damage beyond fair wear and tear by me, an occupant or an invitee` -- s 81E(1)(a), (b)
    `rent or other charges I owe`                                          -- s 81E(1)(c)
    `cleaning what I did not leave reasonably clean`                        -- s 81E(1)(d)
    `replacing locks I changed without consent`                             -- s 81E(1)(e)
    `an amount I owe for breaching the agreement`                           -- s 81E(1)(f)
    `fair wear and tear`                                                    -- excluded from s 81E(1)(a), (b)
    `damage caused by my pet`                                               -- s 81E(2)(a)
    `fumigation because my pet may carry parasites`                         -- s 81E(2)(b)

@export Does the Act entitle my lessor to this from my bond (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 81E)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `A claim on my bond` @desc What the lessor wants paid from the bond
      `my bond includes the pet amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your bond includes the $350 pet amount (s 29(1)(b)(ii))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my lessor entitled to this from my bond` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `fair wear and tear` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `damage caused by my pet` THEN `my bond includes the pet amount`
    WHEN `fumigation because my pet may carry parasites` THEN `my bond includes the pet amount`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 81K(1): "This section applies if each person the bond administrator knows is a party ... (a) makes a security bond release
-- application ...; or (b) agrees to the application under section 81G or otherwise; or (c) ... withdraws the notice [of
-- dispute] under section 81J." s 81K(3): "The bond administrator must pay the security bond to the persons and in the amounts
-- stated in the ... application". s 81I(1): the bond administrator "must refer [the application] to the Commissioner for
-- decision if" it gave notice to another party and that party disputes it, or does not respond in the notice period, or the
-- parties do not otherwise agree in that period.
DECLARE `What happens to my bond release application` IS ONE OF
    `the bond administrator must pay the bond as the application states`
    `it goes to the Commissioner to decide`
    `waiting: the notice period has not ended`

@export What happens to my bond release application (Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 81I, 81K)?
GIVEN `every known party applied, agreed or withdrew their dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every party known to the bond administrator made, agreed to, or stopped disputing the application
      `a party has disputed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another party gave notice of dispute (and has not withdrawn it)
      `the notice period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice period stated by the bond administrator has ended
GIVETH A `What happens to my bond release application`
DECIDE `What happens to my bond application` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `every known party applied, agreed or withdrew their dispute` THEN `the bond administrator must pay the bond as the application states`
      IF `a party has disputed it` OR `the notice period has ended` THEN `it goes to the Commissioner to decide`
      OTHERWISE `waiting: the notice period has not ended`
